---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const post = {
  title: 'Understanding Customer Engagement Metrics',
  date: 'January 1, 2026',
  readTime: '5 min read',
  category: 'Analytics',
  author: 'WATeamInbox Team'
};
---

<Layout title={`${post.title} - WATeamInbox Blog`}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-24 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="text-center">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <span class="rounded-full bg-purple-100 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium text-purple-800">
          {post.category}
        </span>
        <span class="text-gray-500">{post.readTime}</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 md:text-5xl" data-testid="blog-post-title">
        {post.title}
      </h1>
      <div class="mt-6 flex items-center justify-center gap-4 text-gray-600">
        <span>By {post.author}</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <time>{post.date}</time>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Featured Image -->
    <div class="mt-12 flex h-64 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-600 to-purple-800 md:h-96">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-32 w-32 text-white/60" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M9 19v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2zm0 0V9a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v10m-6 0a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v14a2 2 0 01-2 2h-2a2 2 0 01-2-2z" />
      </svg>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-lg mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl" data-testid="blog-post-content">
      <p class="lead text-xl text-gray-600">
        Customer engagement metrics help you understand how well you're connecting with your audience. This guide explains each metric and how to use them to improve your customer relationships.
      </p>

      <h2>The Engagement Score</h2>
      <p>
        The engagement score is a comprehensive metric (0-100) that combines multiple factors to give you an overall picture of customer engagement quality. Higher scores indicate better engagement.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-50 to-indigo-50 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Score Calculation</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">The engagement score is calculated using weighted averages:</p>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-gray-700">Active Contacts Rate</span>
            <span class="font-medium text-purple-600">25%</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-gray-700">Two-Way Conversation Rate</span>
            <span class="font-medium text-purple-600">25%</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-gray-700">Response Rate</span>
            <span class="font-medium text-purple-600">30%</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-gray-700">Media Engagement Rate</span>
            <span class="font-medium text-purple-600">20%</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Key Metrics Explained</h2>

      <h3>Active Contacts Rate</h3>
      <p>
        This measures the percentage of your contacts who have had any activity (sent or received messages) during the selected period. A higher rate indicates a more engaged contact base.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Formula:</strong> (Contacts with activity / Total contacts) × 100</li>
        <li><strong>Good target:</strong> 40-60% for monthly periods</li>
        <li><strong>Action:</strong> Reach out to inactive contacts with relevant updates</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Two-Way Conversation Rate</h3>
      <p>
        This tracks contacts where both parties (you and the customer) have sent messages. Two-way conversations indicate genuine engagement rather than one-sided communication.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Formula:</strong> (Contacts with bidirectional messages / Total active contacts) × 100</li>
        <li><strong>Good target:</strong> 70-80%</li>
        <li><strong>Action:</strong> Ask questions and encourage responses</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Response Rate</h3>
      <p>
        The percentage of inbound messages that received a reply within 24 hours. This is crucial for customer satisfaction and is weighted highest in the engagement score.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Formula:</strong> (Messages with replies within 24h / Total inbound messages) × 100</li>
        <li><strong>Good target:</strong> 90%+ for business accounts</li>
        <li><strong>Action:</strong> Use notifications and team assignments to ensure timely responses</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Media Engagement Rate</h3>
      <p>
        The percentage of conversations that include media (images, videos, documents). Media-rich conversations often indicate deeper engagement.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Formula:</strong> (Conversations with media / Total conversations) × 100</li>
        <li><strong>Good target:</strong> 20-30%</li>
        <li><strong>Action:</strong> Share relevant images, videos, or documents when appropriate</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Reading the Trend Chart</h2>
      <p>
        The engagement trend chart shows your daily engagement scores over time. The bars are color-coded for quick assessment:
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
            <div class="h-8 w-16 rounded bg-green-400"></div>
            <div>
              <span class="font-medium text-gray-900">70+ (High)</span>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Excellent engagement - keep it up!</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
            <div class="h-8 w-16 rounded bg-yellow-400"></div>
            <div>
              <span class="font-medium text-gray-900">40-69 (Medium)</span>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Room for improvement - review response times</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
            <div class="h-8 w-16 rounded bg-red-400"></div>
            <div>
              <span class="font-medium text-gray-900">Below 40 (Low)</span>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Needs attention - check team coverage</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Resolution Rate</h2>
      <p>
        Track how many conversations are being resolved by your team. The resolution rate shows the percentage of conversations marked as resolved versus open or pending.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Conversation States</h4>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4">
          <div class="text-center">
            <div class="mx-auto flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-100">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-6 w-6 text-blue-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 12h.01M12 12h.01M16 12h.01M21 12c0 4.418-4.03 8-9 8a9.863 9.863 0 01-4.255-.949L3 20l1.395-3.72C3.512 15.042 3 13.574 3 12c0-4.418 4.03-8 9-8s9 3.582 9 8z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-2 font-medium text-gray-900">Open</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Active conversations</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <div class="mx-auto flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-yellow-100">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-6 w-6 text-yellow-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-2 font-medium text-gray-900">Pending</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Awaiting action</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <div class="mx-auto flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-green-100">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-6 w-6 text-green-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-2 font-medium text-gray-900">Resolved</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Issue addressed</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Using Metrics to Improve</h2>

      <h3>Daily Review</h3>
      <p>
        Check your engagement score daily to catch issues early. A sudden drop might indicate staffing problems or a surge in customer inquiries.
      </p>

      <h3>Weekly Analysis</h3>
      <p>
        Review trends weekly to identify patterns. Are certain days consistently lower? That might indicate a need for additional coverage.
      </p>

      <h3>Monthly Reports</h3>
      <p>
        Generate monthly reports for stakeholders showing engagement trends, response time improvements, and resolution rates.
      </p>

      <h2>API Access for Custom Reporting</h2>
      <p>
        All engagement metrics are available via our API for custom dashboards and reporting:
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-900 p-4 not-prose my-6">
        <pre class="text-sm text-gray-100 overflow-x-auto"><code>GET /api/analytics/engagement
GET /api/analytics/engagement/trend
GET /api/conversations/stats/resolution</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h2>Conclusion</h2>
      <p>
        Understanding and monitoring customer engagement metrics is essential for delivering excellent customer experiences. Use the engagement score as your north star, but dive into individual metrics to identify specific areas for improvement.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Author Bio -->
    <div class="mt-16 border-t border-gray-200 pt-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <div class="flex h-16 w-16 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-purple-100">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-8 w-8 text-purple-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M16 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0zM12 14a7 7 0 00-7 7h14a7 7 0 00-7-7z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">{post.author}</p>
          <p class="text-gray-600">Building the future of business communication.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Back to Blog -->
    <div class="mt-12 text-center">
      <a href="/blog" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to Blog
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
